    description: "**Defect.** `run_signature` on 30/84 grammar `AnalysisRun` records is hashed from stale pre-mutation config/toolchain values; it is not re-derivable and does not reflect the final config_fingerprint/toolchain.\n\n**Mechanic — ordering bug.** `AnalysisRun.create` (ir.py:254) computes `run_signature = _compute_run_signature(pass_id, version, config_fingerprint, toolchain)` at construction time, using the THEN-current default config_fingerprint (`sha256:44136fa355b3678a`) and default toolchain. AFTERWARD, in `analyze/base.py`, `_extend_toolchain(run)` (base.py:2472) and `_stamp_config_fingerprint(run)` (base.py:2481) MUTATE `run.toolchain` (adding tree_sitter/grammar versions) and `run.config_fingerprint` (deriving a per-analyzer fingerprint) — but `run.run_signature` is NEVER recomputed. So for the 30 grammar-backed analyzers that DO get the mutations, the run_signature is hashed against the pre-mutation basis, contradicting its own config_fingerprint/toolchain fields. Grammar version is also absent from the signature basis.\n\n**Scope.** 30/84 analysis_runs (the grammar-backed `_analyze_body` analyzers that receive the stamping).\n\n**Expectation.** run_signature is a deterministic hash of the FINAL (pass_id, version, config_fingerprint, toolchain) actually recorded on the AR, so a consumer can re-derive it from the AR fields.\n\n**Consequence.** A consumer keying L2 reproducibility / cache invalidation on run_signature cannot reproduce it from the AR's own config_fingerprint+toolchain; two runs differing only in grammar version share a run_signature.\n\n**Unifying fix.** Recompute `run_signature` AFTER `_extend_toolchain` / `_stamp_config_fingerprint` mutate the AR (base.py), and include grammar version in the basis.\n\n**Cross-refs (related, not duplicate).** WI-mipul (the 14 override-`analyze()` analyzers that NEVER get stamped — distinct population & distinct fix); INV-lidul (config_fingerprint default-constant — root of the stale basis but distinct from the recompute-ordering bug); WI-givad (grammar version masked behind one language-pack entry).\n\nMember: F181.A1. Found via dogfooding tranche 10. Severity 4."  # ff19
    fields: {}  # ff19
